# Microsoft Entra ID / MSAL.js — real credentials (NAVIGATION_AND_RBAC.md §3.1).
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored via *.local) and fill in real values.
# App Registration type: SPA, no client secret.
VITE_MSAL_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
VITE_MSAL_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
VITE_MSAL_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4001

# ── Host & TLS (vite.config.ts) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# These four CAN now be set right here in this file (copied to .env.local),
# alongside VITE_MSAL_CLIENT_ID/VITE_MSAL_TENANT_ID above — vite.config.ts calls
# Vite's own `loadEnv()` to read `.env`/`.env.local` in this directory itself,
# since Vite does not put unprefixed vars into `import.meta.env`/process.env on
# its own. A value in the real process environment still wins over the file
# (PowerShell: `$env:TLS_CERT_PATH='C:\path\to\server.pem'; npm run dev`),
# matching dotenv's usual shell-env-beats-file-value precedence.
#
# All four are OPTIONAL. The defaults in vite.config.ts reproduce this laptop's
# original hardcoded dev setup exactly, so local dev needs none of them set.
#
#   HOST           dev-server bind address            default 0.0.0.0 (all NICs)
#   PORT           dev-server port                    default 4001
#   TLS_KEY_PATH   TLS private key, PEM   default frontend/10.10.110.31+1-key.pem
#   TLS_CERT_PATH  TLS certificate, PEM   default frontend/10.10.110.31+1.pem
#
# A relative TLS path resolves against the REPO ROOT (the parent of frontend/) —
# the same base backend/server.ts uses, so one value serves both processes; an
# absolute path is used as-is. The defaults are the mkcert-generated pair
# covering `localhost` + this laptop's static LAN IP; HTTPS is mandatory because
# Entra ID only permits HTTPS redirect URIs for non-`localhost` hosts.
#
# Caveat: PORT here only ever reaches the frontend dev server — `loadEnv()`'s
# envDir is this frontend/ folder, so a PORT set in frontend/.env.local cannot
# reach backend/server.ts (which loads its own, separate backend/.env). The
# pre-existing shared-shell risk is unchanged: `$env:PORT=...` (or root
# `npm run dev`'s combined process environment) still reaches BOTH servers,
# since both read process.env['PORT'] first before falling back to their own
# file. Prefer setting PORT per-process via each side's own .env file, not the
# shared shell, to avoid moving both servers' ports at once.
#
# On another server, register that host's origin as a Redirect URI in the Entra
# App Registration. Nothing in the code needs editing to match: MSAL derives its
# redirectUri from window.location.origin unless VITE_MSAL_REDIRECT_URI overrides
# it, and System > Environment displays that live value so you can copy the exact
# string Entra must allowlist. See backend/.env.example.
